-- coa29-sch5.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), 2006 c. 46, SCHEDULE 5 "Communications by a company".
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Generated by work/build.py from work/src/coa29-sch5.l4; quote lines are produced by srcrefs.py.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter script; it is
-- not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Line numbers are of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- TARGET. The stable `l4` (main) 1.6.110. No section GIVEN, no REFUSE, no sets, no TYPICALLY, no YMD (dates: `Date day month year`).
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the text says the case is within the provision;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words ("may only", a bare "must" not done, an unmet "if", "where" or "to the extent that",
-- a flat negative); NOTHING = the text does not decide (a "may" grant limited by its own wording, a list not closed, silent).
--
-- WHAT THE TEXT LEAVES TO OTHER SECTIONS, each a plain input here: `s 86` (the registered office), `s 112` (member), `s 250` (director),
-- `s 738` (debenture), `s 146` (information rights), `s 18` (the articles), "the register" (see NOTES fork), "hard copy", "electronic
-- form" and "electronic means" (s 1168, the keel), and any "provision of the Companies Acts" that authorises, deems or specifies.
-- A seam input is a MAYBE BOOLEAN named for the answering section (PLAN.md section 4): a NOTHING input never becomes a FALSE here.

§ `Schedule 5 -- Communications by a company`

-- The four forms Part 2 to Part 5 distinguish. The core's `Form of document` has hard copy and electronic form only (NEEDS-CORE.md).
DECLARE `sch 5 form of the document or information` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 hard copy form`
    `sch 5 electronic form`
    `sch 5 made available on a website`
    `sch 5 none of those forms`

-- How the document or information goes: handed to the recipient, by hand to an address, by post, by electronic means, or otherwise.
DECLARE `sch 5 means of sending or supplying` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 handed to the intended recipient`
    `sch 5 by hand to an address`
    `sch 5 by post`
    `sch 5 by electronic means`
    `sch 5 by some other means`

-- What a company does under Part 4 (paragraphs 12 to 14); a typed action for the regulative rules below.
DECLARE `sch 5 action of the company` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 make the document or information available in a form and by a means that enable the recipient to read it and retain a copy`
    `sch 5 notify the intended recipient`
    `sch 5 keep the document or information available on the website throughout the period`

-- Paragraph 14(1): the period throughout which the document or information must be available (first and last day, both included).
DECLARE `sch 5 period of availability` HAS
    `sch 5 first day of the period` IS A DATE
    `sch 5 last day of the period` IS A DATE

§§ `Part 1 -- Introduction`

-- src:19434 | 1 This Schedule applies to documents or information sent or supplied by a company.
@ref sch 5 para 1 Application of this Schedule (src:19434)
GIVEN `the document or information is sent or supplied by a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 1 this Schedule applies to the document or information` MEANS
    IF `the document or information is sent or supplied by a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Schedule applies to documents or information sent or supplied by a company"

§§ `Part 2 -- Communications in hard copy form`

-- src:19442 | (2) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person sends a document or information by post if he posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information.
@ref sch 5 para 3(2) Posting a prepaid envelope (src:19442)
GIVEN `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 3(2) the person sends the document or information by post` MEANS
    IF `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person sends a document or information by post if he posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information"

-- Para 4(1): the addresses to which the company may send hard copy. Limbs (b), (c) and (d) take the answers of s 86, s 112 and s 250
-- as seam inputs; "the register" in (d) is not defined in the paragraph (NOTES fork): the person states that the address is the one shown.
-- src:19444 | 4 (1) A document or information in hard copy form may be sent or supplied by the company—
-- src:19445 | (a) to an address specified for the purpose by the intended recipient;
-- src:19446 | (b) to a company at its registered office;
-- src:19447 | (c) to a person in his capacity as a member of the company at his address as shown in the company's register of members;
-- src:19448 | (d) to a person in his capacity as a director of the company at his address as shown in the register;
-- src:19449 | (e) to an address to which any provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied.
@ref sch 5 para 4(1) Address for communications in hard copy form (src:19444-19449)
GIVEN `the address is specified for the purpose by the intended recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intended recipient is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 112 the person is a member of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the address is shown in the company's register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 250 the person occupies the position of director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the address is shown in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 4(1) the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied by the company` MEANS
    IF       `the address is specified for the purpose by the intended recipient`
         OR  (`the intended recipient is a company` AND `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         OR  (`s 112 the person is a member of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the address is shown in the company's register of members`)
         OR  (`s 250 the person occupies the position of director` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the address is shown in the register`)
         OR  `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be sent or supplied by the company— (a) to an address specified for the purpose by the intended recipient; (b) to a company at its registered office; (c) to a person in his capacity as a member of the company at his address as shown in the company's register of members; (d) to a person in his capacity as a director of the company at his address as shown in the register; (e) to an address to which any provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied"

-- src:19451 | (2) Where the company is unable to obtain an address falling within sub-paragraph (1), the document or information may be sent or supplied to the intended recipient's last address known to the company.
@ref sch 5 para 4(2) The last address known to the company (src:19451)
GIVEN `the company is unable to obtain an address falling within sub-paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is the intended recipient's last address known to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 4(2) the last address known to the company may be used` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is unable to obtain an address falling within sub-paragraph (1)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the company is unable to obtain an address falling within sub-paragraph (1), the document or information may be sent or supplied to the intended recipient's last address known to the company" (a "where" condition not met: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    ELSE IF `the address is the intended recipient's last address known to the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the intended recipient's last address known to the company"

-- Paras 4(1) and 4(2) together: an address to which hard copy may be sent by the company.
-- src:19444 | 4 (1) A document or information in hard copy form may be sent or supplied by the company—
-- src:19445 | (a) to an address specified for the purpose by the intended recipient;
-- src:19446 | (b) to a company at its registered office;
-- src:19447 | (c) to a person in his capacity as a member of the company at his address as shown in the company's register of members;
-- src:19448 | (d) to a person in his capacity as a director of the company at his address as shown in the register;
-- src:19449 | (e) to an address to which any provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied.
-- src:19450 | (1A) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:19451 | (2) Where the company is unable to obtain an address falling within sub-paragraph (1), the document or information may be sent or supplied to the intended recipient's last address known to the company.
@ref sch 5 para 4 Address for communications in hard copy form (sub-paragraphs (1) and (2) together) (src:19444-19451)
GIVEN `the address is specified for the purpose by the intended recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intended recipient is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 112 the person is a member of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the address is shown in the company's register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 250 the person occupies the position of director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the address is shown in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is unable to obtain an address falling within sub-paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is the intended recipient's last address known to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 4 the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied` MEANS
    IF       `sch 5 para 4(1) the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied by the company` `the address is specified for the purpose by the intended recipient` `the intended recipient is a company` `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` `s 112 the person is a member of the company` `the address is shown in the company's register of members` `s 250 the person occupies the position of director` `the address is shown in the register` `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         OR  `sch 5 para 4(2) the last address known to the company may be used` `the company is unable to obtain an address falling within sub-paragraph (1)` `the address is the intended recipient's last address known to the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph 4 lists the addresses to which hard copy "may be sent or supplied" and does not close the list with "only"

-- src:19439 | 3 (1) A document or information in hard copy form must be—
-- src:19440 | (a) handed to the intended recipient, or
-- src:19441 | (b) sent or supplied by hand or by post to an address (in accordance with paragraph 4).
@ref sch 5 para 3(1) Method of communication in hard copy form (src:19439-19441)
GIVEN `the means of sending or supplying` IS A `sch 5 means of sending or supplying`
      `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied under paragraph 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 3(1) the document or information in hard copy form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the means of sending or supplying`
    WHEN `sch 5 handed to the intended recipient` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 by hand to an address` THEN `the address limb`
    WHEN `sch 5 by post` THEN
        IF `sch 5 para 3(2) the person sends the document or information by post` `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN `the address limb`
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document or information in hard copy form must be— (a) handed to the intended recipient, or (b) sent or supplied by hand or by post to an address" (by post is, for this Schedule, posting a prepaid envelope; a bare "must" not done: fork)
    WHEN `sch 5 by electronic means` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be— (a) handed to the intended recipient, or (b) sent or supplied by hand or by post to an address" (a bare "must" not done: fork)
    WHEN `sch 5 by some other means` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be— (a) handed to the intended recipient, or (b) sent or supplied by hand or by post to an address" (a bare "must" not done: fork)
    WHERE
        `the address limb` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied under paragraph 4`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) sent or supplied by hand or by post to an address (in accordance with paragraph 4)" (a bare "must" not done: fork)

-- src:19437 | 2 A document or information is validly sent or supplied by a company if it is sent or supplied in hard copy form in accordance with this Part of this Schedule.
@ref sch 5 para 2 Validly sent by a company in hard copy form (src:19437)
GIVEN `the form of the document or information` IS A `sch 5 form of the document or information`
      `the result of sch 5 para 3(1) the document or information in hard copy form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 2 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in hard copy form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the form of the document or information`
    WHEN `sch 5 hard copy form` THEN
        CONSIDER `the result of sch 5 para 3(1) the document or information in hard copy form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is validly sent or supplied by a company if it is sent or supplied in hard copy form in accordance with this Part of this Schedule" (an unmet "if"; marginal reading (a))
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the method and address of paragraphs 3 and 4 are met is not decided
    WHEN `sch 5 electronic form` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is sent or supplied in hard copy form"
    WHEN `sch 5 made available on a website` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is sent or supplied in hard copy form"
    WHEN `sch 5 none of those forms` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is sent or supplied in hard copy form"

§§ `Part 3 -- Communications in electronic form`

-- src:19456 | 6 A document or information may only be sent or supplied by a company in electronic form—
-- src:19457 | (a) to a person who has agreed (generally or specifically) that the document or information may be sent or supplied in that form (and has not revoked that agreement), or
-- src:19458 | (b) to a company that is deemed to have so agreed by a provision in the Companies Acts.
@ref sch 5 para 6 Agreement to communications in electronic form (src:19456-19458)
GIVEN `the intended recipient is a person who has agreed (generally or specifically) that the document or information may be sent or supplied in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intended recipient has revoked that agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intended recipient is a company deemed by a provision in the Companies Acts to have so agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 6 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company in electronic form` MEANS
    IF       (`the intended recipient is a person who has agreed (generally or specifically) that the document or information may be sent or supplied in electronic form` AND NOT (`the intended recipient has revoked that agreement`))
         OR  `the intended recipient is a company deemed by a provision in the Companies Acts to have so agreed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document or information may only be sent or supplied by a company in electronic form— (a) to a person who has agreed (generally or specifically) that the document or information may be sent or supplied in that form (and has not revoked that agreement), or (b) to a company that is deemed to have so agreed by a provision in the Companies Acts"

-- src:19460 | 7 (1) Where the document or information is sent or supplied by electronic means, it may only be sent or supplied to an address—
-- src:19461 | (a) specified for the purpose by the intended recipient (generally or specifically), or
-- src:19462 | (b) where the intended recipient is a company, deemed by a provision of the Companies Acts to have been so specified.
@ref sch 5 para 7(1) Electronic means: the address (src:19460-19462)
GIVEN `the address is specified for the purpose by the intended recipient (generally or specifically)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intended recipient is a company and a provision of the Companies Acts deems the address to have been so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 7(1) the address is one to which it may be sent or supplied by electronic means` MEANS
    IF       `the address is specified for the purpose by the intended recipient (generally or specifically)`
         OR  `the intended recipient is a company and a provision of the Companies Acts deems the address to have been so specified`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it may only be sent or supplied to an address— (a) specified for the purpose by the intended recipient (generally or specifically), or (b) where the intended recipient is a company, deemed by a provision of the Companies Acts to have been so specified"

-- src:19463 | (2) Where the document or information is sent or supplied in electronic form by hand or by post, it must be—
-- src:19464 | (a) handed to the intended recipient, or
-- src:19465 | (b) sent or supplied to an address to which it could be validly sent if it were in hard copy form.
@ref sch 5 para 7(2) Electronic form by hand or by post (src:19463-19465)
GIVEN `the means of sending or supplying` IS A `sch 5 means of sending or supplying`
      `the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied under paragraph 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 7(2) the document or information in electronic form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the means of sending or supplying`
    WHEN `sch 5 handed to the intended recipient` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 by hand to an address` THEN `the address limb`
    WHEN `sch 5 by post` THEN `the address limb`
    WHEN `sch 5 by electronic means` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the document or information is sent or supplied in electronic form by hand or by post, it must be— (a) handed to the intended recipient, or (b) sent or supplied to an address to which it could be validly sent if it were in hard copy form" (this paragraph is for hand or post; a bare "must" not done: fork)
    WHEN `sch 5 by some other means` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must be— (a) handed to the intended recipient, or (b) sent or supplied to an address to which it could be validly sent if it were in hard copy form" (a bare "must" not done: fork)
    WHERE
        `the address limb` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied under paragraph 4`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) sent or supplied to an address to which it could be validly sent if it were in hard copy form" (a bare "must" not done: fork)

-- src:19454 | 5 A document or information is validly sent or supplied by a company if it is sent in electronic form in accordance with this Part of this Schedule.
@ref sch 5 para 5 Validly sent by a company in electronic form (src:19454)
GIVEN `the form of the document or information` IS A `sch 5 form of the document or information`
      `the result of sch 5 para 6 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company in electronic form` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the means of sending or supplying` IS A `sch 5 means of sending or supplying`
      `the result of sch 5 para 7(1) the address is one to which it may be sent or supplied by electronic means` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result of sch 5 para 7(2) the document or information in electronic form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 5 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in electronic form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the form of the document or information`
    WHEN `sch 5 electronic form` THEN
        IF `the result of sch 5 para 6 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company in electronic form` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN `the address limb`
        ELSE `the answer when para 6 is not JUST TRUE`
    WHEN `sch 5 hard copy form` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is sent in electronic form"
    WHEN `sch 5 made available on a website` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is sent in electronic form"
    WHEN `sch 5 none of those forms` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is sent in electronic form"
    WHERE
        `the address limb` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the means of sending or supplying`
            WHEN `sch 5 by electronic means` THEN `the limb answer` `the result of sch 5 para 7(1) the address is one to which it may be sent or supplied by electronic means`
            WHEN `sch 5 handed to the intended recipient` THEN `the limb answer` `the result of sch 5 para 7(2) the document or information in electronic form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires`
            WHEN `sch 5 by hand to an address` THEN `the limb answer` `the result of sch 5 para 7(2) the document or information in electronic form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires`
            WHEN `sch 5 by post` THEN `the limb answer` `the result of sch 5 para 7(2) the document or information in electronic form is handed over or sent as the paragraph requires`
            WHEN `sch 5 by some other means` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is sent in electronic form in accordance with this Part of this Schedule" (neither paragraph 7(1) nor 7(2); an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        `the limb answer` x MEANS
            CONSIDER x
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is validly sent or supplied by a company if it is sent in electronic form in accordance with this Part of this Schedule" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the paragraph 7 answer is not decided
        `the answer when para 6 is not JUST TRUE` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the result of sch 5 para 6 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company in electronic form`
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document or information may only be sent or supplied by a company in electronic form" (paragraph 6 not met; an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the paragraph 6 answer is not decided
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not reached

§§ `Part 4 -- Communications by means of a website`

-- Para 10: deemed agreement of members and others. The 28 days "beginning with the date" the request was sent include that date.
-- src:19487 | (b) the company has not received a response within the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the company's request was sent.
@ref sch 5 para 10(3)(b) The period of 28 days beginning with the date of the request (src:19487)
GIVEN `the date on which the company's request was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 5 para 10(3)(b) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the request was sent` MEANS
    `the date on which the company's request was sent` PLUS 27

-- src:19490 | (b) was sent less than twelve months after a previous request made to him for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information.
@ref sch 5 para 10(4)(b) Less than twelve months after a previous request (src:19490)
GIVEN `the date on which the company's request was sent` IS A DATE
      `the date on which a previous request was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 10(4)(b) the request was sent less than twelve months after the previous request` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the company's request was sent` LESS THAN (`add months` `the date on which a previous request was sent` 12)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "was sent less than twelve months after a previous request made to him for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information" (twelve months counted by `add months`, which clamps 29 February: fork)

-- src:19491 | (5) Chapter 3 of Part 3 (resolutions affecting a company's constitution) applies to a resolution under this paragraph.
@ref sch 5 para 10(5) Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to the resolution (src:19491)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 10(5) Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution under this paragraph`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to a resolution under this paragraph"

-- src:19477 | 10 (1) This paragraph applies to a document or information to be sent or supplied to a person—
-- src:19478 | (a) as a member of the company, or
-- src:19479 | (b) as a person nominated by a member in accordance with the company's articles to enjoy or exercise all or any specified rights of the member in relation to the company, or
-- src:19480 | (c) as a person nominated by a member under section 146 to enjoy information rights.
-- src:19481 | (2) To the extent that—
-- src:19482 | (a) the members of the company have resolved that the company may send or supply documents or information to members by making them available on a website, or
-- src:19483 | (b) the company's articles contain provision to that effect,
-- src:19484 | a person in relation to whom the following conditions are met is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him in that manner.
-- src:19485 | (3) The conditions are that—
-- src:19486 | (a) the person has been asked individually by the company to agree that the company may send or supply documents or information generally, or the documents or information in question, to him by means of a website, and
-- src:19487 | (b) the company has not received a response within the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the company's request was sent.
-- src:19488 | (4) A person is not taken to have so agreed if the company's request—
-- src:19489 | (a) did not state clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be, or
-- src:19490 | (b) was sent less than twelve months after a previous request made to him for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information.
-- src:19491 | (5) Chapter 3 of Part 3 (resolutions affecting a company's constitution) applies to a resolution under this paragraph.
@ref sch 5 para 10 Deemed agreement of members of company etc to use of website (src:19477-19491)
GIVEN `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as a person nominated by a member in accordance with the company's articles to enjoy or exercise all or any specified rights of the member in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as a person nominated by a member under section 146 to enjoy information rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the members of the company have resolved that the company may send or supply documents or information to members by making them available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles contain provision that the company may send or supply documents or information to members by making them available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company asked the person individually to agree that it may send or supply documents or information generally, or the documents or information in question, to him by means of a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the company's request was sent` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company received a response` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the request stated clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which a previous request was sent for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 10 the person is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` MEANS
    IF NOT (   `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as a member of the company`
            OR `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as a person nominated by a member in accordance with the company's articles to enjoy or exercise all or any specified rights of the member in relation to the company`
            OR `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as a person nominated by a member under section 146 to enjoy information rights`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies to a document or information to be sent or supplied to a person— (a) as a member of the company, or (b) as a person nominated by a member ... or (c) as a person nominated by a member under section 146"
    ELSE IF NOT (   `the members of the company have resolved that the company may send or supply documents or information to members by making them available on a website`
                 OR `the company's articles contain provision that the company may send or supply documents or information to members by making them available on a website`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To the extent that— (a) the members of the company have resolved that the company may send or supply documents or information to members by making them available on a website, or (b) the company's articles contain provision to that effect, a person in relation to whom the following conditions are met is taken to have agreed" (a "to the extent that" condition not met: fork)
         ELSE IF NOT (`the company asked the person individually to agree that it may send or supply documents or information generally, or the documents or information in question, to him by means of a website`)
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are that— (a) the person has been asked individually by the company to agree"
              ELSE IF NOT (`the request stated clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be`)
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not taken to have so agreed if the company's request— (a) did not state clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be"
                   ELSE `the answer once the request was made`
    WHERE
        `the answer once the request was made` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date on which a previous request was sent for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information`
            WHEN JUST previous THEN
                IF `sch 5 para 10(4)(b) the request was sent less than twelve months after the previous request` `the date on which the company's request was sent` previous EQUALS JUST TRUE
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not taken to have so agreed if the company's request— ... (b) was sent less than twelve months after a previous request made to him for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information"
                ELSE `the answer on the response`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the answer on the response`
        `the answer on the response` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date on which the company received a response`
            WHEN JUST received THEN
                IF received AT MOST `sch 5 para 10(3)(b) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the request was sent` `the date on which the company's request was sent`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the company has not received a response within the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the company's request was sent"
                ELSE `the answer once the period has ended`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the answer once the period has ended`
        `the answer once the period has ended` MEANS
            IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `sch 5 para 10(3)(b) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the request was sent` `the date on which the company's request was sent`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period of 28 days has not yet ended, so whether "the company has not received a response within the period" is not yet decided

-- Para 11: debenture holders. The relevant debenture holders and a duly passed resolution are defined in sub-paragraph (5).
-- src:19505 | (a) the relevant debenture holders are the holders of debentures of the company ranking pari passu for all purposes with the intended recipient, and
@ref sch 5 para 11(5)(a) The relevant debenture holders (src:19505)
GIVEN `the holder holds debentures of the company ranking pari passu for all purposes with the intended recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 11(5)(a) the holder is one of the relevant debenture holders` MEANS
    IF `the holder holds debentures of the company ranking pari passu for all purposes with the intended recipient`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant debenture holders are the holders of debentures of the company ranking pari passu for all purposes with the intended recipient"

-- src:19506 | (b) a resolution of the relevant debenture holders is duly passed if they agree in accordance with the provisions of the instruments creating the debentures.
@ref sch 5 para 11(5)(b) A resolution of the relevant debenture holders is duly passed (src:19506)
GIVEN `the relevant debenture holders agree in accordance with the provisions of the instruments creating the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 11(5)(b) the resolution of the relevant debenture holders is duly passed` MEANS
    IF `the relevant debenture holders agree in accordance with the provisions of the instruments creating the debentures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a resolution of the relevant debenture holders is duly passed if they agree in accordance with the provisions of the instruments creating the debentures"

-- src:19500 | (b) the company has not received a response within the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the company's request was sent.
@ref sch 5 para 11(3)(b) The period of 28 days beginning with the date of the request (src:19500)
GIVEN `the date on which the company's request was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 5 para 11(3)(b) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the request was sent` MEANS
    `the date on which the company's request was sent` PLUS 27

-- src:19503 | (b) was sent less than twelve months after a previous request made to him for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information.
@ref sch 5 para 11(4)(b) Less than twelve months after a previous request (src:19503)
GIVEN `the date on which the company's request was sent` IS A DATE
      `the date on which a previous request was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 11(4)(b) the request was sent less than twelve months after the previous request` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the company's request was sent` LESS THAN (`add months` `the date on which a previous request was sent` 12)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "was sent less than twelve months after a previous request made to him for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information" (twelve months counted by `add months`, which clamps 29 February: fork)

-- src:19493 | 11 (1) This paragraph applies to a document or information to be sent or supplied to a person as holder of a company's debentures.
-- src:19494 | (2) To the extent that—
-- src:19495 | (a) the relevant debenture holders have duly resolved that the company may send or supply documents or information to them by making them available on a website, or
-- src:19496 | (b) the instrument creating the debenture in question contains provision to that effect,
-- src:19497 | a debenture holder in relation to whom the following conditions are met is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him in that manner.
-- src:19498 | (3) The conditions are that—
-- src:19499 | (a) the debenture holder has been asked individually by the company to agree that the company may send or supply documents or information generally, or the documents or information in question, to him by means of a website, and
-- src:19500 | (b) the company has not received a response within the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the company's request was sent.
-- src:19501 | (4) A person is not taken to have so agreed if the company's request—
-- src:19502 | (a) did not state clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be, or
-- src:19503 | (b) was sent less than twelve months after a previous request made to him for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information.
-- src:19504 | (5) For the purposes of this paragraph—
-- src:19505 | (a) the relevant debenture holders are the holders of debentures of the company ranking pari passu for all purposes with the intended recipient, and
-- src:19506 | (b) a resolution of the relevant debenture holders is duly passed if they agree in accordance with the provisions of the instruments creating the debentures.
@ref sch 5 para 11 Deemed agreement of debenture holders to use of website (src:19493-19506)
GIVEN `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as holder of the company's debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant debenture holders agree in accordance with the provisions of the instruments creating the debentures that the company may send or supply documents or information to them by making them available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument creating the debenture in question contains provision that the company may send or supply documents or information to debenture holders by making them available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company asked the debenture holder individually to agree that it may send or supply documents or information generally, or the documents or information in question, to him by means of a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the company's request was sent` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company received a response` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the request stated clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which a previous request was sent for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 11 the debenture holder is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the person as holder of the company's debentures`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies to a document or information to be sent or supplied to a person as holder of a company's debentures"
    ELSE IF NOT (   `sch 5 para 11(5)(b) the resolution of the relevant debenture holders is duly passed` `the relevant debenture holders agree in accordance with the provisions of the instruments creating the debentures that the company may send or supply documents or information to them by making them available on a website` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                 OR `the instrument creating the debenture in question contains provision that the company may send or supply documents or information to debenture holders by making them available on a website`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To the extent that— (a) the relevant debenture holders have duly resolved that the company may send or supply documents or information to them by making them available on a website, or (b) the instrument creating the debenture in question contains provision to that effect, a debenture holder in relation to whom the following conditions are met is taken to have agreed" (a "to the extent that" condition not met: fork)
         ELSE IF NOT (`the company asked the debenture holder individually to agree that it may send or supply documents or information generally, or the documents or information in question, to him by means of a website`)
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are that— (a) the debenture holder has been asked individually by the company to agree"
              ELSE IF NOT (`the request stated clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be`)
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not taken to have so agreed if the company's request— (a) did not state clearly what the effect of a failure to respond would be"
                   ELSE `the answer once the request was made`
    WHERE
        `the answer once the request was made` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date on which a previous request was sent for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information`
            WHEN JUST previous THEN
                IF `sch 5 para 11(4)(b) the request was sent less than twelve months after the previous request` `the date on which the company's request was sent` previous EQUALS JUST TRUE
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not taken to have so agreed if the company's request— ... (b) was sent less than twelve months after a previous request made to him for the purposes of this paragraph in respect of the same or a similar class of documents or information"
                ELSE `the answer on the response`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the answer on the response`
        `the answer on the response` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date on which the company received a response`
            WHEN JUST received THEN
                IF received AT MOST `sch 5 para 11(3)(b) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the request was sent` `the date on which the company's request was sent`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the company has not received a response within the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the company's request was sent"
                ELSE `the answer once the period has ended`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the answer once the period has ended`
        `the answer once the period has ended` MEANS
            IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `sch 5 para 11(3)(b) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the request was sent` `the date on which the company's request was sent`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period of 28 days has not yet ended, so whether "the company has not received a response within the period" is not yet decided

-- src:19470 | 9 A document or information may only be sent or supplied by the company to a person by being made available on a website if the person—
-- src:19471 | (a) has agreed (generally or specifically) that the document or information may be sent or supplied to him in that manner, or
-- src:19472 | (b) is taken to have so agreed under—
-- src:19473 | (i) paragraph 10 (members of the company etc), or
-- src:19474 | (ii) paragraph 11 (debenture holders),
-- src:19475 | and has not revoked that agreement.
@ref sch 5 para 9 Agreement to use of website (src:19470-19475)
GIVEN `the person has agreed (generally or specifically) that the document or information may be sent or supplied to him by being made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the result of sch 5 para 10 the person is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result of sch 5 para 11 the debenture holder is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has revoked that agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 9 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company to the person by being made available on a website` MEANS
    IF `the person has revoked that agreement`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be sent or supplied by the company to a person by being made available on a website if the person— ... and has not revoked that agreement" (read as closing both limbs: fork)
    ELSE IF       `the person has agreed (generally or specifically) that the document or information may be sent or supplied to him by being made available on a website`
              OR  `the result of sch 5 para 10 the person is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              OR  `the result of sch 5 para 11 the debenture holder is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF       `the result of sch 5 para 10 the person is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` EQUALS NOTHING
                   OR  `the result of sch 5 para 11 the debenture holder is taken to have agreed that the company may send or supply documents or information to him by means of a website` EQUALS NOTHING
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is taken to have agreed under paragraph 10 or 11 is not decided
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be sent or supplied by the company to a person by being made available on a website if the person— (a) has agreed (generally or specifically) ..., or (b) is taken to have so agreed under— (i) paragraph 10 (members of the company etc), or (ii) paragraph 11 (debenture holders)"

-- src:19508 | 12 (1) A document or information authorised or required to be sent or supplied by means of a website must be made available in a form, and by a means, that the company reasonably considers will enable the recipient—
-- src:19509 | (a) to read it, and
-- src:19510 | (b) to retain a copy of it.
@ref sch 5 para 12(1) Availability of document or information: form and means (src:19508-19510)
GIVEN `the company reasonably considers that the form and means will enable the recipient to read it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company reasonably considers that the form and means will enable the recipient to retain a copy of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 12(1) the document or information has been made available in a form and by a means the paragraph allows` MEANS
    IF       `the company reasonably considers that the form and means will enable the recipient to read it`
         AND `the company reasonably considers that the form and means will enable the recipient to retain a copy of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made available in a form, and by a means, that the company reasonably considers will enable the recipient— (a) to read it, and (b) to retain a copy of it" (a bare "must" not done: fork)

-- src:19511 | (2) For this purpose a document or information can be read only if—
-- src:19512 | (a) it can be read with the naked eye, or
-- src:19513 | (b) to the extent that it consists of images (for example photographs, pictures, maps, plans or drawings), it can be seen with the naked eye.
@ref sch 5 para 12(2) Can be read (src:19511-19513)
GIVEN `it can be read with the naked eye` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it consists of images` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the images can be seen with the naked eye` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 12(2) the document or information can be read` MEANS
    IF       `it can be read with the naked eye`
         OR  (`it consists of images` AND `the images can be seen with the naked eye`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a document or information can be read only if— (a) it can be read with the naked eye, or (b) to the extent that it consists of images (for example photographs, pictures, maps, plans or drawings), it can be seen with the naked eye"

-- src:19515 | 13 (1) The company must notify the intended recipient of—
-- src:19516 | (a) the presence of the document or information on the website,
-- src:19517 | (b) the address of the website,
-- src:19518 | (c) the place on the website where it may be accessed, and
-- src:19519 | (d) how to access the document or information.
@ref sch 5 para 13(1) Notification of availability: what the company must notify (src:19515-19519)
GIVEN `the company notified the intended recipient of the presence of the document or information on the website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company notified the intended recipient of the address of the website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company notified the intended recipient of the place on the website where it may be accessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company notified the intended recipient of how to access the document or information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 13(1) the company has notified the intended recipient as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF       `the company notified the intended recipient of the presence of the document or information on the website`
         AND `the company notified the intended recipient of the address of the website`
         AND `the company notified the intended recipient of the place on the website where it may be accessed`
         AND `the company notified the intended recipient of how to access the document or information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must notify the intended recipient of— (a) the presence of the document or information on the website, (b) the address of the website, (c) the place on the website where it may be accessed, and (d) how to access the document or information" (a bare "must" not done: fork)

-- src:19520 | (2) The document or information is taken to be sent—
-- src:19521 | (a) on the date on which the notification required by this paragraph is sent, or
-- src:19522 | (b) if later, the date on which the document or information first appears on the website after that notification is sent.
@ref sch 5 para 13(2) When the document or information is taken to be sent (src:19520-19522)
GIVEN `the date on which the notification was sent` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the document or information first appears on the website after that notification is sent` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`sch 5 para 13(2) the date on which the document or information is taken to be sent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the document or information first appears on the website after that notification is sent`
    WHEN JUST appears THEN
        IF appears GREATER THAN `the date on which the notification was sent`
        THEN JUST appears
        ELSE JUST `the date on which the notification was sent`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the document or information has not yet appeared on the website after the notification, so the later date in (b) is not known

-- src:19524 | 14 (1) The company must make the document or information available on the website throughout—
-- src:19525 | (a) the period specified by any applicable provision of the Companies Acts, or
-- src:19526 | (b) if no such period is specified, the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the notification required under paragraph 13 is sent to the person in question.
@ref sch 5 para 14(1) Period of availability on website (src:19524-19526)
GIVEN `an applicable provision of the Companies Acts specifies a period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the period so specified` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period so specified` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the notification required under paragraph 13 is sent to the person` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `sch 5 period of availability`
`sch 5 para 14(1) the period throughout which the document or information must be available` MEANS
    IF `an applicable provision of the Companies Acts specifies a period`
    THEN `sch 5 period of availability` WITH
             `sch 5 first day of the period` IS `the first day of the period so specified`
             `sch 5 last day of the period` IS `the last day of the period so specified`
    ELSE `sch 5 period of availability` WITH
             `sch 5 first day of the period` IS `the date on which the notification required under paragraph 13 is sent to the person`
             `sch 5 last day of the period` IS `the date on which the notification required under paragraph 13 is sent to the person` PLUS 27

-- src:19524 | 14 (1) The company must make the document or information available on the website throughout—
@ref sch 5 para 14(1) Must make the document or information available throughout the period (src:19524)
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the first day on which it was available on the website` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which it was available on the website` IS A DATE
      `it was available on every day from the first to the last` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 14(1) the document or information was available on the website throughout the period` MEANS
    IF       `the first day on which it was available on the website` AT MOST `the first day of the period`
         AND `the last day on which it was available on the website` AT LEAST `the last day of the period`
         AND `it was available on every day from the first to the last`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must make the document or information available on the website throughout— ... the period" (a bare "must" not done: fork)

-- src:19527 | (2) For the purposes of this paragraph, a failure to make a document or information available on a website throughout the period mentioned in sub-paragraph (1) shall be disregarded if—
-- src:19528 | (a) it is made available on the website for part of that period, and
-- src:19529 | (b) the failure to make it available throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid.
@ref sch 5 para 14(2) A failure to make it available throughout is disregarded (src:19527-19529)
GIVEN `it was made available on the website for part of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure to make it available throughout the period is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 14(2) the failure to make the document or information available throughout the period is disregarded` MEANS
    IF       `it was made available on the website for part of the period`
         AND `the failure to make it available throughout the period is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a failure to make a document or information available on a website throughout the period ... shall be disregarded if— (a) it is made available on the website for part of that period, and (b) the failure to make it available throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid"

-- src:19524 | 14 (1) The company must make the document or information available on the website throughout—
-- src:19525 | (a) the period specified by any applicable provision of the Companies Acts, or
-- src:19526 | (b) if no such period is specified, the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the notification required under paragraph 13 is sent to the person in question.
-- src:19527 | (2) For the purposes of this paragraph, a failure to make a document or information available on a website throughout the period mentioned in sub-paragraph (1) shall be disregarded if—
-- src:19528 | (a) it is made available on the website for part of that period, and
-- src:19529 | (b) the failure to make it available throughout that period is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid.
@ref sch 5 para 14 The company has kept the document or information available (sub-paragraphs (1) and (2) together) (src:19524-19529)
GIVEN `the result of sch 5 para 14(1) the document or information was available on the website throughout the period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result of sch 5 para 14(2) the failure to make the document or information available throughout the period is disregarded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 14 the company has complied with the duty to keep the document or information available` MEANS
    IF       `the result of sch 5 para 14(1) the document or information was available on the website throughout the period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         OR  `the result of sch 5 para 14(2) the failure to make the document or information available throughout the period is disregarded` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF       `the result of sch 5 para 14(1) the document or information was available on the website throughout the period` EQUALS NOTHING
              OR  `the result of sch 5 para 14(2) the failure to make the document or information available throughout the period is disregarded` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): sub-paragraph (1) or (2) is not decided
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must make the document or information available on the website throughout ... shall be disregarded if" (a bare "must" not done and no disregard: fork)

-- src:19468 | 8 A document or information is validly sent or supplied by a company if it is made available on a website in accordance with this Part of this Schedule.
@ref sch 5 para 8 Validly sent by a company by means of a website (src:19468)
GIVEN `the result of sch 5 para 9 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company to the person by being made available on a website` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result of sch 5 para 12(1) the document or information has been made available in a form and by a means the paragraph allows` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result of sch 5 para 13(1) the company has notified the intended recipient as the paragraph requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result of sch 5 para 14 the company has complied with the duty to keep the document or information available` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 8 the document or information is validly sent or supplied by being made available on a website` MEANS
    IF       `the result of sch 5 para 9 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company to the person by being made available on a website` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         OR  `the result of sch 5 para 12(1) the document or information has been made available in a form and by a means the paragraph allows` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         OR  `the result of sch 5 para 13(1) the company has notified the intended recipient as the paragraph requires` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         OR  `the result of sch 5 para 14 the company has complied with the duty to keep the document or information available` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is validly sent or supplied by a company if it is made available on a website in accordance with this Part of this Schedule" (a paragraph of this Part unmet; an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
    ELSE IF       `the result of sch 5 para 9 the document or information may be sent or supplied by the company to the person by being made available on a website` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `the result of sch 5 para 12(1) the document or information has been made available in a form and by a means the paragraph allows` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `the result of sch 5 para 13(1) the company has notified the intended recipient as the paragraph requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `the result of sch 5 para 14 the company has complied with the duty to keep the document or information available` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a paragraph of this Part is not decided

§§ `Part 4 -- the regulative rules (paragraphs 12(1), 13(1) and 14(1): the company must)`

-- The text gives no time for these duties, so none is written (no WITHIN). The duty is the company's; the correlative claim is the
-- recipient's (NOTES.md, Jural relations). A DEONTIC value cannot be compared in #ASSERT: the tests run these with #TRACE and the
-- decision functions above carry the same duties as asserted rules.
-- src:19508 | 12 (1) A document or information authorised or required to be sent or supplied by means of a website must be made available in a form, and by a means, that the company reasonably considers will enable the recipient—
-- src:19509 | (a) to read it, and
-- src:19510 | (b) to retain a copy of it.
@ref sch 5 para 12(1) The company must make it available in a form and by a means that enable the recipient to read it and retain a copy (src:19508-19510)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sch 5 action of the company`
`sch 5 para 12(1) the company must make the document or information available so that the recipient can read it and retain a copy` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `sch 5 make the document or information available in a form and by a means that enable the recipient to read it and retain a copy`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not make the document or information available in a form and by a means that it reasonably considers will enable the recipient to read it and to retain a copy of it"

-- src:19515 | 13 (1) The company must notify the intended recipient of—
-- src:19516 | (a) the presence of the document or information on the website,
-- src:19517 | (b) the address of the website,
-- src:19518 | (c) the place on the website where it may be accessed, and
-- src:19519 | (d) how to access the document or information.
@ref sch 5 para 13(1) The company must notify the intended recipient (src:19515-19519)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sch 5 action of the company`
`sch 5 para 13(1) the company must notify the intended recipient of the document or information on the website` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `sch 5 notify the intended recipient`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not notify the intended recipient of the presence of the document or information on the website, the address of the website, the place on the website where it may be accessed and how to access it"

-- src:19524 | 14 (1) The company must make the document or information available on the website throughout—
-- src:19525 | (a) the period specified by any applicable provision of the Companies Acts, or
-- src:19526 | (b) if no such period is specified, the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the notification required under paragraph 13 is sent to the person in question.
@ref sch 5 para 14(1) The company must make it available on the website throughout the period (src:19524-19526)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sch 5 action of the company`
`sch 5 para 14(1) the company must keep the document or information available on the website throughout the period` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `sch 5 keep the document or information available on the website throughout the period`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not make the document or information available on the website throughout the period"

§§ `Part 5 -- Other agreed forms of communication`

-- src:19531 | 15 A document or information that is sent or supplied otherwise than in hard copy or electronic form or by means of a website is validly sent or supplied if it is sent or supplied in a form or manner that has been agreed by the intended recipient.
@ref sch 5 para 15 Other agreed forms of communication (src:19531)
GIVEN `the form of the document or information` IS A `sch 5 form of the document or information`
      `the form or manner has been agreed by the intended recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 15 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in another agreed form or manner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the form of the document or information`
    WHEN `sch 5 none of those forms` THEN
        IF `the form or manner has been agreed by the intended recipient`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is validly sent or supplied if it is sent or supplied in a form or manner that has been agreed by the intended recipient" (an unmet "if"; marginal reading (a))
    WHEN `sch 5 hard copy form` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "otherwise than in hard copy or electronic form or by means of a website"
    WHEN `sch 5 electronic form` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "otherwise than in hard copy or electronic form or by means of a website"
    WHEN `sch 5 made available on a website` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "otherwise than in hard copy or electronic form or by means of a website"

§§ `Part 6 -- Supplementary provisions`

-- src:19534 | 16 (1) This paragraph applies in relation to documents or information to be sent or supplied to joint holders of shares or debentures of a company.
-- src:19535 | (2) Anything to be agreed or specified by the holder must be agreed or specified by all the joint holders.
@ref sch 5 para 16(2) Joint holders: what is agreed or specified (src:19534-19535)
GIVEN `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to joint holders of shares or debentures of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of joint holders` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of joint holders who agreed or specified the matter` IS A NUMBER
      `the company's articles contain provision to a different effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 16(2) the matter is agreed or specified by the joint holders as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the document or information is to be sent or supplied to joint holders of shares or debentures of a company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies in relation to documents or information to be sent or supplied to joint holders of shares or debentures of a company"
    ELSE IF `the company's articles contain provision to a different effect`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "This paragraph has effect subject to anything in the company's articles" (the articles are not among the sources)
         ELSE IF `the number of joint holders who agreed or specified the matter` AT LEAST `the number of joint holders`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Anything to be agreed or specified by the holder must be agreed or specified by all the joint holders"

-- src:19536 | (3) Anything authorised or required to be sent or supplied to the holder may be sent or supplied either—
-- src:19537 | (a) to each of the joint holders, or
-- src:19538 | (b) to the holder whose name appears first in the register of members or the relevant register of debenture holders.
@ref sch 5 para 16(3) Joint holders: to whom the document or information may be sent (src:19536-19538)
GIVEN `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to joint holders of shares or debentures of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent or supplied to each of the joint holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent or supplied to the holder whose name appears first in the register of members or the relevant register of debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles contain provision to a different effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 16(3) the document or information may be sent or supplied to the joint holder` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the document or information is to be sent or supplied to joint holders of shares or debentures of a company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies in relation to documents or information to be sent or supplied to joint holders of shares or debentures of a company"
    ELSE IF `the company's articles contain provision to a different effect`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "This paragraph has effect subject to anything in the company's articles" (the articles are not among the sources)
         ELSE IF       `it is sent or supplied to each of the joint holders`
                   OR  `it is sent or supplied to the holder whose name appears first in the register of members or the relevant register of debenture holders`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be sent or supplied either— (a) to each of the joint holders, or (b) to the holder whose name appears first in the register of members or the relevant register of debenture holders"

-- Para 17(5): references to bankruptcy "include" sequestration and an estate that is the subject of a protected trust deed.
DECLARE `sch 5 para 17(5) event affecting the holder` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 para 17(5) bankruptcy in the ordinary sense`
    `sch 5 para 17(5) sequestration of the estate of a person`
    `sch 5 para 17(5) a person's estate being the subject of a protected trust deed`
    `sch 5 para 17(5) some other insolvency event`

-- src:19549 | (5) References in this paragraph to the bankruptcy of a person include—
-- src:19550 | (a) the sequestration of the estate of a person;
-- src:19551 | (b) a person's estate being the subject of a protected trust deed (within the meaning of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016).
-- src:19552 | In such a case the reference in sub-paragraph (2)(b) to the trustee of the bankrupt is to be read as the trustee or interim trustee (under that Act) on the sequestrated estate or, as the case may be, the trustee under the protected deed.
@ref sch 5 para 17(5) References to bankruptcy include (src:19549-19552)
GIVEN event IS A `sch 5 para 17(5) event affecting the holder`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 17(5) the event is bankruptcy for the purposes of the paragraph` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `sch 5 para 17(5) bankruptcy in the ordinary sense` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 17(5) sequestration of the estate of a person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 17(5) a person's estate being the subject of a protected trust deed` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 para 17(5) some other insolvency event` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this paragraph to the bankruptcy of a person include— (a) the sequestration of the estate of a person; (b) a person's estate being the subject of a protected trust deed"

-- src:19542 | 17 (1) This paragraph has effect in the case of the death or bankruptcy of a holder of a company's shares.
-- src:19543 | (2) Documents or information required or authorised to be sent or supplied to the member may be sent or supplied to the persons claiming to be entitled to the shares in consequence of the death or bankruptcy—
-- src:19544 | (a) by name, or
-- src:19545 | (b) by the title of representatives of the deceased, or trustee of the bankrupt, or by any like description,
-- src:19546 | at the address in the United Kingdom supplied for the purpose by those so claiming.
@ref sch 5 para 17(2) Death or bankruptcy of a holder of shares: who may be sent the document or information (src:19542-19546)
GIVEN `the holder of the company's shares has died or become bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or information is sent to the persons claiming to be entitled to the shares in consequence of the death or bankruptcy by name or by the title of representatives of the deceased, or trustee of the bankrupt, or by any like description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent at the address in the United Kingdom supplied for the purpose by those so claiming` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles contain provision to a different effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 17(2) the document or information may be sent or supplied to the persons claiming to be entitled` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the holder of the company's shares has died or become bankrupt`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph has effect in the case of the death or bankruptcy of a holder of a company's shares"
    ELSE IF `the company's articles contain provision to a different effect`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "This paragraph has effect subject to anything in the company's articles" (the articles are not among the sources)
         ELSE IF       `the document or information is sent to the persons claiming to be entitled to the shares in consequence of the death or bankruptcy by name or by the title of representatives of the deceased, or trustee of the bankrupt, or by any like description`
                   AND `it is sent at the address in the United Kingdom supplied for the purpose by those so claiming`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be sent or supplied to the persons claiming to be entitled to the shares ... at the address in the United Kingdom supplied for the purpose by those so claiming"

-- src:19547 | (3) Until such an address has been so supplied, a document or information may be sent or supplied in any manner in which it might have been sent or supplied if the death or bankruptcy had not occurred.
@ref sch 5 para 17(3) Until the address has been supplied (src:19547)
GIVEN `the holder of the company's shares has died or become bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those claiming to be entitled have supplied an address in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent or supplied in a manner in which it might have been sent or supplied if the death or bankruptcy had not occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles contain provision to a different effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 17(3) the document or information may be sent or supplied in the manner that applied before the death or bankruptcy` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the holder of the company's shares has died or become bankrupt`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph has effect in the case of the death or bankruptcy of a holder of a company's shares"
    ELSE IF `the company's articles contain provision to a different effect`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "This paragraph has effect subject to anything in the company's articles" (the articles are not among the sources)
         ELSE IF `those claiming to be entitled have supplied an address in the United Kingdom`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Until such an address has been so supplied, a document or information may be sent or supplied in any manner in which it might have been sent or supplied if the death or bankruptcy had not occurred" (an "until" bar ended: ruling of 2026-11-05)
              ELSE IF `it is sent or supplied in a manner in which it might have been sent or supplied if the death or bankruptcy had not occurred`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any manner in which it might have been sent or supplied if the death or bankruptcy had not occurred"
